00:29:13,226 --> 00:29:15,770
creating a better picture of the epidemic

497
00:29:15,770 --> 00:29:18,773
and freeing up time for patient care.

498
00:29:20,066 --> 00:29:21,359
The power to affect

499
00:29:21,359 --> 00:29:24,320
the real world makes safety even more important.

500
00:29:24,904 --> 00:29:27,573
It's why Claude's full biology capabilities

501
00:29:27,573 --> 00:29:30,576
go only to organizations we've verified.

502
00:29:32,537 --> 00:29:35,540
And why Claude has a constitution.

503
00:29:36,040 --> 00:29:40,336
It equips it to make judgment calls in situations it has never encountered

504
00:29:40,336 --> 00:29:42,380
before.

505
00:29:42,380 --> 00:29:47,135
And it's why we put so much energy into interpretability and alignment.

506
00:29:47,343 --> 00:29:51,681
To keep Claude accountable in situations where people will rely on it

507
00:29:52,807 --> 00:29:53,808
again and again.

508
00:29:53,808 --> 00:29:56,435
We're finding safety doesn't hold us back.

509
00:29:56,435 --> 00:29:59,480
In fact, it's because we can trust Claude's work

510
00:29:59,564 --> 00:30:03,109
that we can take its discoveries and apply them in the real world

511
00:30:04,235 --> 00:30:07,238
in ways that will benefit everyone.

512
00:30:11,325 --> 00:30:14,370
We believe the transformation of the global economy through

513
00:30:14,412 --> 00:30:17,540
AI is the greatest economic opportunity in history.

514
00:30:17,665 --> 00:30:20,376
And Anthropic is uniquely positioned to capture it.

515
00:30:20,376 --> 00:30:23,462
We have leadership at the frontier of AI, where we expect value

516
00:30:23,504 --> 00:30:26,507
will differentially accrue, and the strength of our business model

517
00:30:26,549 --> 00:30:29,510
allows us to keep investing to advance the frontier

518
00:30:29,510 --> 00:30:33,639
while delivering more value to customers and superior returns for our shareholders.

519
00:30:33,639 --> 00:30:36,642
The clearest evidence of that is our financial results.

520
00:30:36,684 --> 00:30:39,896
In Q3, we earned nearly $17 billion

521
00:30:39,896 --> 00:30:43,065
of revenue, up 12 times year over year. And year to date,

522
00:30:43,107 --> 00:30:46,027
we've delivered a compute margin of 43%,

523
00:30:46,027 --> 00:30:48,070
gross margin of 85%,

524
00:30:48,070 --> 00:30:51,949
adjusted operating margin of 12% and positive free cash flow.

525
00:30:52,491 --> 00:30:55,328
These results come from our frontier leadership,

526
00:30:55,328 --> 00:30:58,456
and they give us the capacity to invest heavily to extend it.

527
00:30:58,456 --> 00:31:02,418
So while our profitability is strong, we are in an aggressive investment

528
00:31:02,418 --> 00:31:05,546
mode as we focus on building this business for the long term.

529
00:31:05,755 --> 00:31:09,133
There are five elements that differentiate Anthropic's business model.

530
00:31:09,175 --> 00:31:13,221
First, we build models that deliver the most useful intelligence

531
00:31:13,346 --> 00:31:14,680
as we've pushed the frontier.

532
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:17,516
Our customers have found more valuable work for Claude.

533
00:31:17,516 --> 00:31:19,477
And our revenue growth has followed.

534
00:31:19,477 --> 00:31:21,479
We call this model led growth.

535
00:31:21,479 --> 00:31:23,981
The trajectory of our business demonstrates this.

536
00:31:23,981 --> 00:31:28,694
Quarterly revenue grew from $376 million in Q1 2025

537
00:31:29,070 --> 00:31:32,490
to nearly $17 billion in Q3 of 2026.

538
00:31:32,865 --> 00:31:36,410
This tracks significant increases in the capabilities of our models

539
00:31:36,410 --> 00:31:40,414
in coding workflows and real world tasks.

540
00:31:40,748 --> 00:31:44,543
Being at the frontier unlocks new use cases and capabilities.

541
00:31:44,585 --> 00:31:48,673
It also moves us towards Pareto dominance across most customer workloads,

542
00:31:48,798 --> 00:31:52,969
enabling us to deliver the most capable models at a given cost.

543
00:31:53,094 --> 00:31:56,055
That is because smarter models are more efficient.

544
00:31:56,055 --> 00:32:00,476
They can complete tasks at lower effort levels, which use fewer tokens.

545
00:32:00,643 --> 00:32:04,814
We also cascade the frontier intelligence from our larger models

546
00:32:04,897 --> 00:32:06,482
into our smaller models.

547
00:32:06,482 --> 00:32:10,695
So we address the full range of cost, capability and speed.

548
00:32:11,070 --> 00:32:13,781
Each generation has pushed that further.

549
00:32:13,781 --> 00:32:16,701
Our recent Claude 5.5 family of models are a

550
00:32:16,701 --> 00:32:20,162
significant step up in capability from the Claude 5 family

551
00:32:20,204 --> 00:32:22,123
we released just a few months prior.

552
00:32:22,123 --> 00:32:25,334
They're also significantly cheaper on a cost per task basis.

553
00:32:25,459 --> 00:32:28,337
That is the power of building at the frontier.

554
00:32:28,337 --> 00:32:32,008
We believe we deliver the highest value intelligence at the lowest cost,

555
00:32:32,133 --> 00:32:34,969
which means we can serve the entire market efficiently.

556
00:32:34,969 --> 00:32:38,931
While we lead across most benchmarks, the true measure of our success

557
00:32:39,432 --> 00:32:40,599
is our customers.

558
00:32:40,599 --> 00:32:43,602
And that leads me to our second differentiator.

559
00:32:44,020 --> 00:32:46,981
We build the leading platform and products to make

560
00:32:46,981 --> 00:32:49,984
frontier intelligence accessible to our customers.

561
00:32:50,151 --> 00:32:53,654
Our platform solutions are the foundation of our business,

562
00:32:53,988 --> 00:32:57,700
and there is significant opportunity for customers to build products

563
00:32:57,700 --> 00:33:01,412
and reimagine processes on top of our APIs and SDK.

564
00:33:01,829 --> 00:33:06,042
At the same time, our own products have become a key driver of diffusion.

565
00:33:06,208 --> 00:33:07,168
For example,

566
00:33:07,168 --> 00:33:11,714
Claude Code was fundamentally a bet on the exponential in model progress.

567
00:33:11,839 --> 00:33:15,760
Getting it into the hands of our customers put us in a position to capitalize

568
00:33:15,760 --> 00:33:19,221
on agentic coding capabilities as they dramatically improved.

569
00:33:19,430 --> 00:33:23,309
We followed that same playbook with Claude Cowork, and its adoption

570
00:33:23,309 --> 00:33:26,312
has exceeded that of Claude Code at the equivalent point,

571
00:33:26,312 --> 00:33:28,522
following its own research preview last year.

572
00:33:28,522 --> 00:33:33,319
Together, our products and platform enable us to serve the needs of our customers.

573
00:33:33,486 --> 00:33:37,656
Today, the majority of enterprise customers use both our platform

574
00:33:37,698 --> 00:33:42,536
and at least one of our products, up from 30% in the fourth quarter of 2025.

575
00:33:42,703 --> 00:33:47,375
Our product velocity is also accelerating as we expand our internal use of Claude.

576
00:33:47,458 --> 00:33:51,295
The average daily volume of code contributed per engineer is up

577
00:33:51,295 --> 00:33:54,423
45x relative to the 2024 average,

578
00:33:54,423 --> 00:33:58,469
and that's showing up in our launches. In the first nine months of 2026,

579
00:33:58,594 --> 00:34:02,056
we shipped 250 models, products and features.

580
00:34:02,348 --> 00:34:06,310
And Claude isn't just accelerating our engineering teams across the company.

581
00:34:06,435 --> 00:34:10,272
Our employees' use of Claude grew more than 250 times

582
00:34:10,314 --> 00:34:13,317
between January and September of 2026.

583
00:34:13,359 --> 00:34:17,238
Together, these help explain why our revenue per employee has grown

584
00:34:17,238 --> 00:34:22,076
more than 4.5x from $1.4 million in Q3 of 2025

585
00:34:22,201 --> 00:34:25,955
to over $6.6 million as of Q3 2026.

586
00:34:25,996 --> 00:34:30,668
Anthropic's third differentiator is that we are extremely efficient users of compute.

587
00:34:30,751 --> 00:34:34,755
We treat our compute as one fungible pool that serves customers,

588
00:34:34,839 --> 00:34:38,092
trains our models and powers our own use of Claude.

589
00:34:38,217 --> 00:34:41,387
We are focused on getting the most out of every unit of compute.

590
00:34:42,138 --> 00:34:45,558
This gives us a cost to serve and a reinvestment advantage.

591
00:34:45,850 --> 00:34:49,186
As Tom described, there are two drivers of this efficiency.

592
00:34:49,728 --> 00:34:53,107
The first is our multi-silicon strategy, which lets us

593
00:34:53,107 --> 00:34:57,111
buy the most price-performant chips and run them as a single fungible pool.

594
00:34:57,194 --> 00:35:01,824
The second is compounding compute multipliers, which have scaled our total

595
00:35:01,824 --> 00:35:05,744
effective compute significantly faster than our physical capacity.

596
00:35:06,287 --> 00:35:09,915
You can see this in our financial results over the last six quarters.

597
00:35:09,999 --> 00:35:14,086
We grew revenue by more than 45x, while computing infrastructure costs

598
00:35:14,086 --> 00:35:17,423
grew only 10x, a more than 4x improvement

599
00:35:17,423 --> 00:35:20,426
in revenue per dollar of compute. And year to date,

600
00:35:20,551 --> 00:35:23,679
our gross margin has improved to over 85%,

601
00:35:23,929 --> 00:35:27,266
up from 29% in the same period of 2025.

602
00:35:27,349 --> 00:35:31,270
We think of these efficiency gains as capital that we get to allocate.

603
00:35:31,479 --> 00:35:35,357
In some cases, we pass them along to customers by lowering prices,

604
00:35:35,399 --> 00:35:38,527
which drives diffusion of Claude across those customers.

605
00:35:38,736 --> 00:35:42,072
In other cases, we retain the margin and reinvest it

606
00:35:42,072 --> 00:35:45,784
in additional compute, which is what makes this advantage compound.

607
00:35:45,910 --> 00:35:50,456
The next differentiator is our relentless focus on building for enterprises.

608
00:35:50,748 --> 00:35:54,710
We had the early insight that enterprises would be the largest and best customers

609
00:35:54,710 --> 00:35:55,669
for AI.

610
00:35:55,669 --> 00:35:59,298
We have focused on serving that market since our commercial launch

611
00:35:59,298 --> 00:36:02,885
in the first quarter of 2023, and have seen rapid adoption

612
00:36:02,885 --> 00:36:05,888
since. As of Q3 2026,

613
00:36:05,930 --> 00:36:09,725
we had more than 11,900 enterprise customers, up

614
00:36:09,725 --> 00:36:11,810
nearly 8x from the start of the year.

615
00:36:11,810 --> 00:36:15,105
As the first frontier lab available on all three major clouds,

616
00:36:15,397 --> 00:36:18,359
we allow enterprises to deploy Claude within the environments

617
00:36:18,359 --> 00:36:19,610
they already operate in,

618
00:36:19,610 --> 00:36:22,530
and we maintain the direct relationship with the end customer,

619
00:36:22,530 --> 00:36:24,406
including control over pricing.

620
00:36:24,406 --> 00:36:27,535
We believe these partnerships enable us to be far more efficient

621
00:36:27,535 --> 00:36:30,162
in our go-to-market efforts than the rest of the industry.

622
00:36:30,162 --> 00:36:33,874
In fact, our entire non-compute expense base, including sales

623
00:36:33,874 --> 00:36:37,628
and marketing personnel and other operating expenses, represents

624
00:36:37,628 --> 00:36:40,589
a lower percentage of revenue than the median enterprise

625
00:36:40,589 --> 00:36:43,592
software company spends on sales and marketing alone.

626
00:36:43,592 --> 00:36:47,054
We expect to invest meaningfully in go-to-market to support our growth,

627
00:36:47,388 --> 00:36:51,267
while remaining highly efficient in how we sell to and grow with our customers.

628
00:36:51,350 --> 00:36:54,520
Our final differentiator is our expanding market opportunity.

629
00:36:55,229 --> 00:36:58,566
We believe every company, across every industry

630
00:36:58,774 --> 00:37:01,318
will be transformed by powerful AI.

631
00:37:01,318 --> 00:37:03,737
It started with coding and is spreading to knowledge

632
00:37:03,737 --> 00:37:07,908
work, a $40 trillion market that we have just begun to penetrate.

633
00:37:08,325 --> 00:37:12,830
We count many of the world's largest and most complex businesses as our customers,

634
00:37:13,038 --> 00:37:18,002
including over 50% of the Fortune 500 and over 30% of the Global 2000.

635
00:37:18,043 --> 00:37:23,465
And as Paul described, our Fortune 500 customers spend less than 0.1%

636
00:37:23,549 --> 00:37:27,761
of their total expenses on Claude. As the frontier of AI advances,

637
00:37:28,012 --> 00:37:31,181
we expect it will open up entirely new lines of business.

638
00:37:31,348 --> 00:37:34,643
This has started already with cybersecurity, and we expect it

639
00:37:34,643 --> 00:37:37,980
will extend to life sciences and robotics in the coming years.

640
00:37:38,230 --> 00:37:42,526
Given the size of the opportunity we see and the strength of our business,

641
00:37:43,152 --> 00:37:46,739
we are investing aggressively in three areas: compute,

642
00:37:47,323 --> 00:37:50,326
customer value and safety and alignment.

643
00:37:50,492 --> 00:37:53,495
Compute is a critical enabler of our growth.

644
00:37:53,537 --> 00:37:57,708
It powers our R&D and enables us to meet expanding customer demand.

645
00:37:57,958 --> 00:38:01,378
We plan to make significant investments in compute over the coming years,

646
00:38:01,462 --> 00:38:05,090
given the compelling returns we see. That includes both short-term

647
00:38:05,090 --> 00:38:09,595
and multi-year cloud deals as well as data centers and chips we lease directly.

648
00:38:09,637 --> 00:38:12,931
We call this last piece Anthropic Direct, and we expect

649
00:38:12,931 --> 00:38:16,226
it will make up a growing share of our compute base over the coming years.

650
00:38:16,685 --> 00:38:19,688
Our second investment area is customer value.

651
00:38:19,813 --> 00:38:22,858
We are maniacally focused on ensuring customers

652
00:38:22,858 --> 00:38:25,861
get the strongest return from their spend on Claude.

653
00:38:25,986 --> 00:38:30,783
We do this through developing the most capable, aligned and useful models

654
00:38:30,949 --> 00:38:34,578
and through reducing customer costs as we make our models more efficient.

655
00:38:34,662 --> 00:38:39,124
For example, our Opus 5.5 model in September delivered substantial gains

656
00:38:39,124 --> 00:38:42,795
in model capability and 40% lower customer costs.

657
00:38:42,878 --> 00:38:46,590
This reduction was margin neutral to us because Opus 5.5

658
00:38:46,632 --> 00:38:48,592
is significantly cheaper to serve.

659
00:38:48,592 --> 00:38:52,221
While we sacrifice some near-term revenue when we reduce customer costs,

660
00:38:52,429 --> 00:38:55,808
in our experience, we quickly see a tailwind to revenue

661
00:38:55,891 --> 00:39:00,020
as the lower cost of intelligence drives greater usage and diffusion of Claude.

662
00:39:00,396 --> 00:39:03,232
The third area is safety and alignment.

663
00:39:03,232 --> 00:39:06,068
Safety is core to how we operate at Anthropic,

664
00:39:06,068 --> 00:39:09,113
and we've been investing here since the inception of the company.

665
00:39:09,196 --> 00:39:11,615
As model capabilities advance rapidly,

666
00:39:11,615 --> 00:39:14,743
we're investing even more in people, processes

667
00:39:14,743 --> 00:39:17,746
and compute to support our safety and alignment work.

668
00:39:17,830 --> 00:39:22,710
Taken together, we expect our focus on safety to remain a commercial advantage

669
00:39:22,876 --> 00:39:26,463
because customers and developers want models and products they can trust.

670
00:39:26,588 --> 00:39:30,968
The investments we're making in compute, customer value and safety and alignment

671
00:39:30,968 --> 00:39:35,097
will strengthen our business and broaden our opportunity over the long term.

672
00:39:35,347 --> 00:39:40,102
We believe Anthropic can deliver adjusted operating margins of more than 35%,

673
00:39:40,144 --> 00:39:43,689
with continued efficiency gains, a greater share of Anthropic

674
00:39:43,689 --> 00:39:47,359
Direct capacity, and more of our compute shifting towards inference.

675
00:39:47,401 --> 00:39:50,404
We see a path for compute and infrastructure expenses

676
00:39:50,404 --> 00:39:53,782
to trend towards approximately 45 to 50% of revenue.

677
00:39:54,366 --> 00:39:57,619
Second, we expect sales, marketing and partnership costs

678
00:39:57,619 --> 00:40:00,038
to trend towards 7 to 10% of revenue,

679
00:40:00,038 --> 00:40:03,208
as partner fees become a smaller share of revenue as we scale.

680
00:40:03,625 --> 00:40:07,296
And third, we expect personnel and other operating expenses

681
00:40:07,296 --> 00:40:10,466
combined to trend towards 7 to 10% of revenue,

682
00:40:10,549 --> 00:40:14,803
as Claude makes our teams more productive and we grow headcount efficiently.

683
00:40:14,845 --> 00:40:18,098
We believe we have the best financial model: leading compute

684
00:40:18,098 --> 00:40:21,643
efficiency, the greatest concentration of talent, and a culture

685
00:40:21,643 --> 00:40:25,522
that keeps us focused on where we can add the most value to enterprises.

686
00:40:25,773 --> 00:40:30,194
AI's transformation of the global economy has the potential to be the largest

687
00:40:30,194 --> 00:40:34,031
economic opportunity in history, and we are at the foothills of it today.

688
00:40:38,035 --> 00:40:39,411
You know, if today we look

689
00:40:39,411 --> 00:40:43,832
at things like cancer, Alzheimer's, heart disease,

690
00:40:44,249 --> 00:40:48,879
mental illness, these will be relics of the past

691
00:40:49,087 --> 00:40:52,049
in, I think, less than a decade.

692
00:40:52,049 --> 00:40:55,636
And I believe that the company which gets the risks right

693
00:40:55,677 --> 00:40:59,848
will also be the company that has the license to operate

694
00:40:59,848 --> 00:41:04,853
that society trusts and society believes can build the benefits in the right way.

695
00:41:05,437 --> 00:41:09,733
I think if we do this right, we can create an age of miracles

696
00:41:09,733 --> 00:41:14,321
where humanity is able to solve problems

697
00:41:14,488 --> 00:41:17,699
that have eluded us for millennia.

698
00:41:17,950 --> 00:41:21,495
We have to make sure that all the risks,

699
00:41:21,703 --> 00:41:24,706
all the ways that things can go wrong with this technology,

700
00:41:24,706 --> 00:41:27,876
we very carefully address those risks

701
00:41:28,085 --> 00:41:32,005
as we bring the benefits, and as we have a viable business at the same time.

702
00:41:32,089 --> 00:41:36,218
And I invite you to join us on the next phase of this journey.
